	"system": {
		"description": "<p>Every Champion must have a cause: a person, a government, a source of power, or an ideal to which they hold and gain some measure of their resolve. At 1st level, choose from one of the following options:</p><p><strong>Arena Fighter:</strong> When you use rise to the challenge, you may choose two offensive targets. When you hinder one you also hinder the other, so long as both are within range.</p><p><strong>Knight of the Realm:</strong> You are able to move up to half speed before using your offensive and defensive reaction abilities. This applies to your mounted speed, if you have one.</p><p><strong>Guardian of Nature:</strong> You may help or hinder your defensive or offensive targets so long as they are within the normal range of your readied ranged weapon. Doing so costs 1 ammunition per use.</p><p><strong>Noble Protector:</strong> If your defensive target is within 10ft of you, their AC is increased by half of your proficiency bonus, rounded down.</p><p><strong>Noblesse Oblige:</strong> When you use rise to the challenge, you may choose two defensive targets. When you help one you also help the other, so long as both are within range.</p><p><strong>Supernatural Patron:</strong> You gain the Warlock’s Eldritch Scythe ability. You may use your eldritch scythe twice per round at 5th level and 3 times per round at 10th level. You use Strength on your Scythe attacks.</p><p><strong>Temple Protector:</strong> As a bonus action, you may expend 1 hit die and grant the resulting hit points to your defensive target if they are within 5ft as healing.</p>",
